From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code (Opus 5) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 03:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 23/26] cuda: fuse the exact Nemotron router and top-k dispatch

Ported from the Nemotron R9700 HIP series to the GB10 CUDA track. Both tracks
pin llama.cpp 0b1bad14ff20 and llama.cpp's HIP backend is the CUDA backend
source-translated, so the diff applies to ggml/src/ggml-cuda unchanged.

Keep the stock F32 MMVF router reduction and its logits materialization, and
let the last producer block run the mechanically identical stock top-6 warp,
removing the dependent top-k dispatch without reordering the graph.

Wave-width safe by construction: the launcher refuses the fusion unless the
device warp size equals WARP_SIZE, and the per-thread expert count is
n_experts/WARP_SIZE, so 128 experts become 4 per lane on CUDA where they are
2 per lane on wave64.

GB10 leave-one-out: GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_NEMO_ROUTER_TOPK_FUSION=1 costs 0.22%.
---
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh
